# Frontend Rules

Use React functional components.

Use TypeScript strict typing.

The frontend displays analytical results.

It does not calculate analytical results.

Never reproduce backend scoring formulas in TypeScript.

Never infer missing metrics in the frontend.

Use structured API fields instead of parsing numbers from LLM-generated text.

Keep server communication inside services/api.ts.

Use TanStack Query where server-state management helps.

Use local React state for simple UI state.

Do not introduce Redux.

Components should be grouped by domain:

chat/
airport/
common/
layout/

Create reusable components only when reuse is real.

Avoid giant components.

Prefer composition over deeply configurable components.

Display:

- confidence
- assumptions
- warnings
- sources

when supplied by the backend.

Voice functionality must always have a text fallback.

Do not automatically execute uncertain speech recognition results.

Keep the visual design minimal, professional and readable.

Before adding a new frontend component, check docs/CODEBASE_MAP.md for the appropriate component group.